About
A spontaneous side/fun project, not a serious product build - an idea that came up on a whim.
This repository contains a pure input/output "bedieneinheit" (HMI panel) built with ESPHome
for Home Assistant. It targets an Olimex ESP32-POE-ISO driving an MPR121 capacitive touch
sensor (12 touch zones: digits 0-9 plus dedicated ARM/DISARM) and an RGB edge-lit backlight
(2 LEDs shining into the laser-cut acrylic edge, lighting up the engraved symbols instead of
individual status LEDs). All alarm logic - PIN validation, arm/disarm state, door contacts,
entry delay, siren, lockout, users - lives in Home Assistant, not on the device.
Idea: build it into a JUNG LS 990 single-gang cover with the face plate fully closed,
symbols only laser-engraved over the touch pads, no through-holes anywhere.
Status: concept / work in progress, notes not a build guide - see README.md
"Open Questions / Roadmap" for what's still undecided (OLED fit, exact touch zone layout,
custom PCB, the HA-side package).

Important Notice
This project was created with the help of AI-assisted development.
No warranty is provided for correctness, safety, or fitness for production use.
Use at your own risk.
